    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1510">

                <pb facs="1218" n="1102" xml:id="pg1102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/450.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Wands transmits from Paris the recommendation yesterday of the French
                    bondholders’ committee to accept plan for settlement of the 1909 loan
                    question.</p>
                <p>Similar action yesterday by the committee of the council of foreign bondholders
                    of London.</p>
                <p>Wands requests that Schoenrich be informed that the matter he referred to in
                    letter of April 13 can probably be arranged.</p>
                <p>At the Department yesterday Mallet-Prévost seemed hopeful of early relief for
                    Nicaragua.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
